>From http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/wizmode.txt :

  ^W  make wish.

      You can wish for any object in the game and get it, including the
      invocation items and the Amulet of Yendor; your Quest Artifact (and
      other artifacts, with no chance of failure); magic lamps; usable
      wands of wishing; and venom. You can specify any valid attribute on
      an object, and get it (regardless of Luck or other factors), even
      ones you can't usually wish for (charges, enchantments and quantities
      in excess of their usual limits, and "trapped" chests). You can also
      wish for traps by name, and some dungeon features: fountains ("magic"
      can be specified), thrones, sinks, pools, lava, altars (of a
      particular alignment, or random if you don't specify), graves, trees,
      and iron bars.


(Note that that still leaves plenty of dungeon features you _can't_
wish for: walls, doors, drawbridges, stairs, ladders, ice,
clouds... if you want to test the behaviour of these, it's generally a
matter of just going where you know they'll be (or creating your own,
in the case of ice).)

